      "writtenOn": "2026-04-22T10:34:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a way we could ASSERT that we don\u0027t forget to call a `SetQueryAvailable` somewhere in the backends? Or is the idea to rely on end2end tests to check that?\n\nBut also the information of which querysets are to be made available is already in the PassResourceUsage in the `QuerySetToSlotUsageMap`. So instead, we could have a frontend function that takes that map and marks all the queries in it available. Then the backends would call it at the start of each pass. It avoids manually adding code to all the backend code paths that make queries available, which should be less error prone.",
      "revId": "398f499709cec476147eb6d2261ce01ceab7f2bf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
