        "id": 1003446
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-23T05:50:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So I made that version here: https://dawn-review.googlesource.com/c/dawn/+/304596, but I ran into the issue that you need to track slot usage between passes.\n\nIn other words\n   \n```\nencoder \u003d createEncoder()\npass1 \u003d encoder.createComputePass(slots(1,2))\npass1.end()\nencoder.WriteTimestamp(slot(3))\nencoder.WriteTimestamp(slot(4))\nencoder.ResolveQuerySet(slots(7,8))   \u003c---------- (A) error\npass2 \u003d encoder.createComputePass(slots(5,6))\npass2.end();\nencoder.WriteTimestamp(slot(7))       \u003c---------- (B) because\nencoder.WriteTimestamp(slot(8))\nqueue.submit(encoder.finish());\n```\n\nCurrently each pass keeps it\u0027s own slot usage which it can apply before the pass starts and you can\u0027t call ResolveQuerySet within a pass. But, the command encoder (commands outside of passes) can also issue WriteTimestamp And ResolveQuerySet. At each ResolveQuerySet, you\u0027d need to save off the current querySetToUsedSlotMap and start a fresh one so that a (A) above, only slots 1,2,3,4 are marked as available.\nWithout that, slots 7,8 also get marked as available when the entire command buffer starts.",
      "parentUuid": "0f045e81_062094ad",
      "revId": "398f499709cec476147eb6d2261ce01ceab7f2bf",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
